<onlyinclude>'''Silicon''' is a chemical element used to make many computer chips and solar cells. In a carefully grown crystal, its electrical behavior can be controlled by adding tiny amounts of other elements. Silicon is the starting material; a working chip requires many additional manufacturing steps.</onlyinclude>

== Why silicon is useful ==
Pure crystalline silicon conducts electricity differently from a metal or an insulator. Adding small amounts of boron or phosphorus changes which electrical charges are available to move. Engineers combine differently treated regions to build electronic components.

Silicon also forms silicon dioxide, an insulating material that can protect surfaces and separate electrical structures. Not all silicon looks or behaves the same: single crystals, polycrystalline silicon and amorphous silicon have different uses.

== What to remember ==
A silicon wafer is not already a processor. Fabrication patterns many layers and electrical connections onto it. Its electronic properties also change with temperature.

